Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): provider in-app notification feed with unread
 badge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds /provider/notifications — an owner-scoped, newest-first in-app feed and
an 'Alerts' unread badge in the provider nav, so providers see application
decision updates in the product without depending on any email/vendor setup.

Frontend-only: consumes the existing MC8-lite APIs (GET /providers/notifications
keyset-paginated, GET .../unread-count, idempotent POST .../:id/read) via the
generated client. Handles loading/empty/error+retry/401/403/pagination and
mark-read (optimistic + rollback + failure toast); read-state stays server-owned.

No backend, schema, OpenAPI, generated-client, lifecycle-event, or notification
-semantics changes. No email/SMTP/push/SSE/notification-bus/vendor coupling
(complies with the notification channel-abstraction constraint).

Scope: artifacts/web/ + .agents traceability. Verified via typecheck, build,
API regression (reviewer-decisions 14/14, provider-notifications 12/12), and
manual browser screenshots (no web test framework introduced).
